ay\":\"3800\",\"perKM\":\"14\"}]'),(17,'2005-11-24 05:45:00','2024-11-07 06:08:25','Car Rental In Bageshwar',10,'car-rental-in-bageshwar','<h1>Duracabs Car Rental in Bageshwar</h1><p>Dura Cabs Services Provides You a best car hire &amp; rental service in Bageshwar with Memorable moments and hassle-free journey. U are makes a relationship for ever for all Needs of Travel Services in india. We are offer you Car rental in Bageshwar, Car hire service in Bageshwar, car on rent/hire in Bageshwar, taxi service Bageshwar, taxi for outstaion in Bageshwar, wedding car rental in Bageshwar, india tour package etc. Our cab such as Toyota Etios, innova, Crysta, wagonr, maruti ritz, swift dezire, ciaz as well chauffeur drive.</p><h3>Bageshwar</h3><p>Situated at the convergence of the river Saryu, the Gomti, and the idle Bhagirathi, is the holy township of Bageshwar; Also known as the holy land associated with Lord Sadashiv, the savior of all sins. As stated in the Puranas, it is indeed a place capable of liberating one from the eternal slavery of birth and death. Adjacent to Bhileshwar and Nileshwar mountains in the east and west and surrounded by Suraj Kund in the north and Agni Kund in the south, this land of Lord Shankar is of great religious, primeval, and political importance.</p><h3>Pindari and Sunderdhunga Glaciers</h3><p>Pindari and Sunderdhunga Glaciers are the ideal spots to go touring If you\'re an adventure traveler. While touring Pindari Glacier is considered easy than going to Sunderdhunga Glacier, both have ceaseless beauty to bait you through stirring trekking adventures. Pindari Glacier is located just by the hem of Nanda Devi and is on a height of 3353mts. On the other hand, Sunderdhunga Glacier lies on the right of Pindar and both glaciers offer a fantastic view of Himalayan lookouts that isn\'t to be missed if you\'re then in Bageshwar.</p><h3>Baghnath Temple</h3><p>Baghnath Temple is actually the central shrine on which this city is named. It\'s located at the joining of the two sacred rivers of Gomti and Saryu. This shrine is devoted to Lord Shiva and is the place where he meditated in Bageshwar. It was constructed in 1450 by Laxmi Chand, a Kumaon King. The best time to visit this temple is during the Hindu jubilee of Shivratri when a joyful festivity is organized then drawing excursionists from all around India.</p><h3>Chandika Temple</h3><p>Chandika Temple is the holy shrine devoted to the Hindu deity Chandika Mai also referred to as Maa Kali. It is merely a half-kilometer from Bageshwar and attracts tourists, especially during the months of Navrataras. Further, Goddess Chandika Mai is a revered deity for the locals here and thus is a must-place to visit in Bageshwar and experience the divine tranquility this place possesses.</p><h3>Baijnath</h3><p>Located at a distance of 26 km from Bageshwar, Baijnath is an important place of interest, known for its early sanctuaries and named after the famous Baijnath temple then situated. Baijnath actually served as the capital during the time of the Katyuri lords during the 7th to 11th-century annals and its earlier name was Kartikeyapura located in the Katyur valley. The Baijnath temple was also built by the Katyuri kings enlarging the icons of Lord Shiva, Goddess Parvati, Lord Ganesha, Lord Brahma, and colorful other Hindu deities. Also, it is primarily dedicated to Lord Shiva, and as per Hindu mythology, it is said that the marriage of Lord Shiva and Goddess Parvati took place at the river Gomti and Garur Ganges.</p><p><br></p>','page',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Car Rental In Bageshwar: Cabs in Bageshwar Rs.9km only','Duracabs offerCar Rental In Bageshwar service 24x7. you book cabs in Bageshwar online for local and out stations trip from Bageshwar at very lowest prices.',NULL,'cab service in bagheshwar,taxi service,taxi service in bagheshwar,cab service,taxi service near me,car rental agencies in bagheshwar,one way cab taxi,taxi cab online booking,car rental with driver,airpor