rnal comes from Karnalaya, where Alaya means residence. Mahabharata’s generality is embedded in the names of the utmost of Haryana’s sections. This not only means that the Mahabharata’s knowledge is embedded in the veritably social fabric of the people then, but also that the region is in a fascinating position to study the epic. Karnal is no exception indeed. Present-day Karnal still, offers an imagery of lush fields, Basmati, artificial geography, educated service class, and a quiet and peaceful megacity. It has come synonymous with the National Highway 44( NH- 44), which is popularly known as GT Karnal Road( Grand Box Karnal Road). Lying the interior between Delhi and Chandigarh, ultramodern day Karnal is invested with the culture of both the metropolises. Indeed though the megacity has witnessed changing political centers, much of its soul has remained unchanged. It\'s framed by Kurukshetra( northwest), Jind and Kaithal( west), and Panipat( south). On the east, it\'s separated from Uttar Pradesh through the Yamuna, which also forms a natural border between the two countries. Karnal has come to a mature quarter after independence.</p><h3>Cantonment Church Tower</h3><p>Being a fine example of the unique architectural style of the British era, Cantonment Church Tower stands tall in Karnal and it was built in 1806 AD. This tourist attraction is placed around one kilometer from Liberty Chowk towards Karnal and Indian National Trust for Art and Cultural Heritage has certified this Cantonment Church Tower to be a historic monument of the country.</p><h3>Qualander Shah’s Tomb</h3><p>Built-in the memory of Bo-Ali-Qualander Shah, the famous Muslim sage, this place of honour was constructed by Ghias-ud-din Tughlaq, the ruler of Delhi and this well-sculptured grave is made of marble.</p>','page',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'Car Rental In Karnal: Cabs in Karnal Rs.9/km only','Duracabs offerCar Rental In Karnal service 24x7. you book cabs in Karnal online for local and out stati