apital of two states, Punjab and Haryana. It is also a Union Territory, which means it is directly governed by the central government of India.</p><h3>Places to Visit in Chandigarh Private Cab</h3><p>The city is divided into various sectors, each with its own markets, schools, and residential areas. The Capitol Complex, which houses the government buildings of Punjab and Haryana, is one of the city\'s most famous landmarks. Other popular tourist attractions in Chandigarh include the Rock Garden, Sukhna Lake, Rose Garden, and the International Dolls Museum.</p><p><strong><br>Rock Garden<br></strong><br></p><p>The Rock Garden is a unique sculpture garden made of recycled materials like rocks, broken bangles, and discarded ceramics. Created by artist Nek Chand, it is one of the most visited tourist places in Chandigarh.</p><p><strong><br>Sukhna Lake<br></strong><br></p><p>Sukhna Lake is a man-made lake located in the foothills of the Himalayas. It is a popular spot for boating, jogging, and picnicking. The lake is also home to various species of birds, making it a great place for birdwatching.</p><p><strong><br>Rose Garden<br></strong><br></p><p>The Zakir Hussain Rose Garden is Asia\'s largest rose garden, with over 17,000 rose bushes of 1,600 different species. The garden is a beautiful sight to behold, especially during the annual rose festival, which attracts thousands of visitors every year.</p><p><strong><br>Capitol Complex<br></strong><br></p><p>The Capitol Complex is a group of government buildings designed by renowned architect Le Corbusier. It includes the Secretariat, High Court, and Legislative Assembly buildings, and is a must-visit for architecture enthusiasts.</p><p><strong><br>Pinjore Gardens<br></strong><br></p><p>The Pinjore Gardens are a beautiful Mughal-style garden located on the outskirts of Chandigarh. They are known for their stunning water fountains, pavilions, and terraced lawns.</p><p><strong><br>Cactus Garden<br></strong><br></p><p>The Cactus