k of the river. It is 692 kilometers (430 mi) to the southeast of India\'s capital New Delhi and 320 kilometers (200 mi) to the east of the state capital, Lucknow. It lies 121 kilometers (75 mi) downstream of Prayagraj, where the confluence with the Yamuna River is another major Hindu pilgrimage site.</p><p><br></p>',NULL,NULL,1,0,1,1,'none','Agra to Varanasi Cab/Taxi Hire Oneway Rs.11317','Hire Agra To Varanasi cab online at the best price. Duracabs provides the most affordable and reliable cab service on this route. Price starts at Rs.11317',NULL,NULL,1,1,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2025-10-13 06:24:33','2025-10-13 06:24:33'),(110,1,'with_driver','car',1,111,'Agra,Uttar Pradesh To Vrindavan,Uttar Pradesh','agra-uttar-pradesh-to-vrindavan-uttar-pradesh','seo_page','route','one_way',1980.00,2218.00,65.00,7.00,9.00,150.00,0.00,0.00,0.00,'[\"products\\/01JACF9VVJ6NR66H0XWR9XVVQQ.jpg\"]','<h1>Agra to Vrindavan Cab Hire</h1><p><strong>Agra to Vrindavan cab</strong> is the most convenient way to get there if you are planning a pilgrimage to Vrindavan. It is simple and comfortable to take a <strong>cab from Agra to Vrindavan</strong>, which will let you explore the city\'s holy atmosphere without bothering about public transport inconveniences. Vrindavan, one of India\'s most visited pilgrim spots lies near Agra. In India, this is known as one of the holiest of cities and has been extremely popular with visitors who go there for spiritual reasons. It is thought by many that it was in this place where Lord Krishna was born; he was a very much respected Hindu deity.</p><h2>What are the benefits of taking a cab from Agra to Vrindavan?</h2><p>The primary benefit of taking an Agra to Vrindavan cab is the convenience it offers. Taking a cab from Agra to Vrindavan eliminates the need for you to worry about public transportation, which can be unreliable and time-consuming. Taking a cab from Agra to Vrindavan also gives you the freedom to plan your own route, as you\'l